=== TITLE: Color Doppler Scrotum (Varicocele & Testicular Study) ===
=== IMPRESSION ===
NORMAL SCROTAL ULTRASOUND AND COLOR DOPPLER STUDY.
- Bilateral testes and epididymides are normal in size, echotexture, and vascularity.
- No evidence of varicocele, hydrocele, or testicular space-occupying lesion.

=== FINDINGS ===
STUDY: HIGH-RESOLUTION ULTRASOUND & COLOR DOPPLER OF SCROTUM

OBSERVATIONS:
- RIGHT TESTIS: Normal in size (4.2 x 2.4 x 2.8 cm), shape, and position. Homogeneous parenchymal echotexture. No focal solid or cystic mass lesion. Normal intra-testicular arterial flow on Color Doppler.
- LEFT TESTIS: Normal in size (4.1 x 2.3 x 2.7 cm), shape, and position. Uniform echotexture. No focal lesion seen. Normal vascularity.
- EPIDIDYMIDES: Bilateral epididymal heads, bodies, and tails appear normal in size, shape, and echogenicity. No epididymal cyst or inflammatory changes.
- PAMPINIFORM PLEXUS:
  * Right: Normal caliber (1.6 mm at rest). No venous dilatation or retrograde reflux on Valsalva maneuver.
  * Left: Normal caliber (1.7 mm at rest). No venous dilatation or retrograde reflux on Valsalva maneuver.
- SCROTAL SAC & SPERMATIC CORDS: Scrotal wall thickness is normal. No hydrocele, hematocele, or inguinal hernia on either side.